{"seq":2,"slug":"deepening-daoism","title":"Deepening Daoism","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/core-contributions/deepening-daoism","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"beyond-laozi","title":"超越老子","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/core-contributions/deepening-daoism/beyond-laozi","wordCount":1622,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-philosophy-of-freedom","title":"自由的哲学","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/core-contributions/deepening-daoism/the-philosophy-of-freedom","wordCount":1743,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<p>本章呈现庄子对道家思想的深化与超越。庄子虽继承老子，却以独立的精神超越了老子——他将道家的关注焦点，从社会政治转向了个体的精神自由，将道家追求自由的精神推向了极致。庄子的哲学，本质上是一种&quot;自由的哲学&quot;——以追求精神的绝对自由（无待的逍遥）为核心与灵魂。本章揭示庄子作为道家发展者的独特贡献。</p>\n"}